<div class="markup-toc-wrapper">
<button class="markup-toc-button">Show Table of Contents</button></div>Welcome to Wowhead's Best in Slot Gear list for Restoration Druid Healer in Cataclysm Classic Phase 4. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Dragon Soul, Firelands, Twilight Protocol Dungeons, and Valor Points. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">
<span class="c11">Best in Slot Gear for Restoration Druid Healer in Phase 4</span></h2>Resto Druids see a few major changes to itemization in Cataclysm: all HoTs can now crit, Haste affects all HoTs tick rate, and MP5 is no longer a stat (replaced by Spirit). The latter doesn't really matter as very little of our gear had MP5 to begin with, but it does change some items.<br/>
<br/>However, most importantly, Cataclysm brings armor specialization - which means that wearing all Leather grants us 5% extra Intellect (which is also Spell Power in Cataclysm). That means it's time to throw all of that gross Cloth, Leather is in back in fashion.<br/>
<br/>Overall, our primary gearing goal will be to pinpoint our Haste breakpoints (916 or 2005) while accumulating as much Intellect as possible. Then, balance our mana regen with Spirit. Afterwards, Mastery tends to be slightly stronger than Crit Rating point for point. Due to the stat totals available, once you have reached 359 ilvl, hitting the 2005 haste breakpoint should be manageable. In full raid BiS, it's expected that your setup should always be at the 2005 haste breakpoint.<br/>
<br/>The biggest change in gear options is that the Cataclysm "healer only" stat, Spirit, is much better than the Wrath "healer only" stat, MP5, and is also much more widely available. For this minor tradeoff, we need to compete with select hybrid DPS for Spirit gear: Shadow Priest, Elemental Shaman, and Balance Druid. But, that's a small price to pay for having way more gear availability. In general, it should be much easier to gear up as a healer in Cataclysm than any previous classic expansion.<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Intellect </b>- Now gives Spell Power by itself on top of the Mana and Crit Rating that it provided in Wrath. We now gem for Intellect (it's a red gem now), unless you're trying to hit a specific Haste breakpoint.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Spirit </b>- Our core regeneration stat. The 5 second rule is completely gone in Cataclysm, there's only "in combat" and "out of combat" regen.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Haste </b>- Now affects all of our HoT tick rates by default. At specific breakpoints, you gain extra ticks with different HoTs, and is the primary focus of Haste for Resto Druids in Cataclysm. The breakpoints we want to focus on are 916 and 2005. Between breakpoints, Haste is a mana-negative, healing-positive stat, but will find just as many situations where you lose value as you gain value by quickening the tick rate. It is recommended to tailor gear to have just enough Haste, and reforge or gem for more throughput stats.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Mastery </b>- A new stat that buffs all of our direct healing. Additionally <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=77495/harmony">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/classic_spell_nature_healingway.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Harmony</span></a> also buffs all HoTs an equal amount as long as you cast enough direct heals to keep the buff active. For healing throughput exclusively, this is a great stat.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Critical Strike</b> - All of our HoTs can now crit, making this no longer a dead stat. Critical healing also now does 200% healing in Cataclysm, up from 150% in previous expansions. Since the stat budget of critical strike rating on gear is pretty expensive, it's less effective for healing throughput increases than Mastery.</div></li></ol>
<div class="wh-center" style="text-align: -webkit-center;">
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="bis-phase-4">BiS Phase 4</h4>This is the best possible setup in Phase 4 and will set you up very comfortable to heal in Dragon Soul. <br/>Many slots have limited options this phase, but its still important to remember that the haste off-piece alternatives are very close in value. You can choose whichever item is available to you and adjust based on your current haste situation.<br/>
